hput 500 req/s for peak trading-support scenarios.\nModel preferences: prefer Open Llama 70B quantized variant for embeddings/reranking and a smaller 13B chat model for conversational assistants; fallback to hosted lightweight models during maintenance windows.\nCost sensitivity: high \u2014 looking to trade small increases in latency for significant token-cost reductions via quantization and caching. Interested in Redwood Optimize recommendations.\nCompliance asks: SOC2 report required, ISO27001 desired, contractual language for data residency (EU-only for production dataset) and right-to-audit clauses.\nQuote from CTO on 2026-02-19 demo: 'We need absolute proof that customer tokens never leave EU compute \u2014 show us keys + telemetry.'\nRecent risk: Legal flagged clause around cross-border model telemetry; asking for explicit telemetry redaction and per-tenant telemetry filters.\nPOC plan: 4-week private VPC PoC \u2014 week 1 network & IAM setup, week 2 KMS + audit logging, week 3 performance tuning (batching/caching), week 4 security pen-test and final report.\nThey provided vendor comparators: AWS Bedrock offering looked easier for SSO onboarding but lacked clear audit log export; Anthropic had stronger safety docs but no EU-dedicated private offering in their stack.\nInternal champions: Head of ML ops (Laura Hendricks) and Senior Security Engineer (Marc Dubois). AE says both are very engaged.\nRequested artifacts shared: security FAQ, sample KMS integration guide, Private VPC checklist (links in Drive).\nNotes style: fragmented; action items highlighted in next_step and blockers.\nComplete encryption & KMS integration design; schedule legal sign-off call w/ security team\nLegal sign-off on EU-only residency language\nInternal budget commit for Dedicated capacity\nSAML IdP metadata pending (Okta)\n2026-01-20: Intro discovery call (AE Morgan Lee) \u2014 reviewed high-level architecture and residency needs\n2026-02-19: Demo with ML infra + SE team (Priya) \u2014 showed private VPC prototype; CTO on call\n2026-02-24: Security questionnaire submitted by Harbor; Redwood responded 2026-02-26\n2026-03-02: Deep-dive on KMS + audit logging (SE + InfoSec) \u2014 action: produce KMS design doc\n2026-03-05: Legal asked for contractual residency language; AE raised to GTM lead\n2026-03-09: Follow-up call \u2014 agreed on 4-week PoC scope and success criteria (signed MoM)."
